    },
    {
      "title": "Eknath Shinde meets PM Modi in Delhi, discusses Maharashtra drought",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/eknath-shinde-meets-pm-modi-in-delhi-discusses-maharashtra-drought-126100501265_1.html",
      "description": "Maharashtra Deputy Chief Minister Eknath Shinde met Prime Minister Narendra Modi on Monday, during which the latter assured the Centre's support in tackling the drought.\nSpeaking to reporters in New Delhi, Shinde said Modi held an extensive discussion on the drought situation in Maharashtra and enquired about the status of water, fodder, and crop damage.\nThe meeting lasted an hour, said an aide of Shinde.\nThe Maharashtra government on September 26 declared drought in 265 of its 358 talukas, or 74 per cent of the state, amid rainfall deficit.\nShinde's meeting with Modi comes in the backdrop of a tussle between the Mahayuti allies Shiv Sena and the BJP over the MLC election for the Pune Teachers Constituency, a seat for which both the parties have announced candidates.\nShinde said PM Modi sought details on water availability, agricultural conditions and fodder for livestock and assured the state of the Centre's support.\nThe Deputy CM expressed confidence that substantial assistance",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-05T18:55:45"
    }
